cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FLINT, please cite the version you used."
title: "FLINT: Flow-INtegrity Tracking — flow-typed provenance security for LLM agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jones
    given-names: Nicholas
    affiliation: Torrens University Australia
version: 0.3.1
date-released: "2026-10-03"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickjones39/FLINT"
abstract: >-
  FLINT consumes LLM-agent execution provenance captured as W3C PROV and
  detects prompt injection as an information-flow property: untrusted-origin
  data reaching a privileged action along a path with no authorised
  endorsement. It ships the flow detector, a fail-closed loader for
  deployment, and an evasion testbed showing that structural graph attacks
  cannot silence the detector; only attacks on the trust labels can.
keywords:
  - provenance
  - W3C PROV
  - prompt injection
  - LLM agents
  - information flow
